# Normalize line endings for source.
* text=auto

# Artifacts whose bytes are their identity.
#
# `maxey0-ss.app.artifact` and `/health` publish a sha256 of the MCP App, and
# the edge copy is asserted byte-identical to the origin copy by
# `test_edge_app_artifact_is_byte_identical_to_the_origin`. Under `text=auto`
# git would check these out with CRLF on Windows, changing the digest and
# failing that assertion on a fresh clone. Treat them as binary.
workers/mcp-edge/src/generated/super-space.html -text
mcp_apps/super_space_react/dist/mcp-app.html    -text
mcp_apps/super_space.html                       -text

# Files executed inside the Linux image. A Windows checkout under `text=auto`
# would give deploy/entrypoint.sh CRLF endings, and `#!/bin/sh\r` fails at
# container start with a bare "not found" -- after the deploy has already
# replaced the running Machine. The Dockerfile also refuses a CRLF entrypoint.
*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
